post_install() {
  cat << 'EOFMSG'
==> TAPE 24 has been installed.

Main command:
    tape24

The official Linux build is X11-backed. On a Wayland session it runs
through XWayland. The launcher sources:
    /usr/share/tape24/profiles/tape24-wayland.env   (Wayland login)
    /usr/share/tape24/profiles/tape24-x11.env       (X11 login)

Config and logs:
    ~/.config/TapeDAW/TAPE 24/
    UI defaults are stored in ui-preferences.txt

Command-line tools:
    tape24-plugin-doctor
        Internal plugin diagnostic helper.
        Logs: ~/.config/TapeDAW/TAPE 24/

    tape24-reset-defaults
        Reset UI/workflow preferences (timestamped backup).
        Does not remove licenses, sessions, recordings or plugins.
        Optional: tape24-reset-defaults --include-plugin-cache

    In the app UI, similar actions are in Plugin Manager:
        Deep Rescan, UNSCAN, Reset Plugin System

Audio:
    TAPE 24 talks JACK (libjack). The launcher prefers JACK and, when
    available, starts the app through pw-jack.
    Recommended: PipeWire + pipewire-jack + wireplumber
    Alternative: jack2
    Set the device and buffer in TAPE 24 Audio Settings.
    Optional: pacman -S realtime-privileges
              sudo usermod -aG realtime $USER
              then log out and back in

Wayland sessions:
    pacman -S xorg-xwayland

Control surfaces (FaderPort, Console 1, Mackie/MCU, etc.):
    Appear as ALSA MIDI ports. Select them in TAPE 24 MIDI / controller
    settings. No extra udev rules are shipped.

Video (optional):
    Movie playback uses GStreamer.
    pacman -S gst-plugins-good gst-libav

Updates:
    Update this install through the AUR helper (pacman/yay/paru).
    The in-app CHECK UPDATE / AUTO UPDATE flow talks to GitHub and
    offers the official .deb/.AppImage, which would bypass this
    package. Leave AUTO UPDATE off in Support, or ignore those offers.

Optional launch flags:
    TAPE16_SURGE_EDITOR_MODE=isolated tape24
        Isolated Surge XT editor if the native window is blank.

    TAPE16_PREFER_NATIVE_WAYLAND=1 tape24
        Experimental. Not recommended by upstream.

Remote:
    Enabled by default on the local network (TAPE16_REMOTE_LAN=1).
    Disable with: TAPE16_REMOTE_LAN=0 tape24

    The QR code encodes http://IP:PORT/remote/#token=...
    If that IP is wrong (VPN, VM bridge, etc.), open the URL and
    replace the IP with this machine's address on the same network
    as your phone.

    Do not enable this on public or untrusted Wi-Fi.

More info:
    https://wiki.archlinux.org/title/PipeWire
    https://wiki.archlinux.org/title/Realtime_process_management
EOFMSG
}

post_upgrade() {
  post_install
}
